    "what_this_means": "Judge didn't just pile on runs. He converted traffic that the lineup had already created. Cam Schlittler was sharp (1.52 ERA entering this game), holding Baltimore to one run across 5.2 innings, but it was Judge's two-run homer and two-run single that turned a workmanlike game into a 12-1 blowout. The offense produced ten hits; Judge made them count. Jazz Chisholm Jr. started the eighth-inning rally with a single, but that moment mattered only because Judge had already given them air. This is a team that executes when both sides click. Pitching tight, offense decisive. And when that alignment holds, the margin becomes real. The formula doesn't just work. It doesn't have competition when everything's there. Four RBIs in one night doesn't define a season. But it defines how this team wins when it's winning.",
